--TEST--
A `...` or a default on an anonymous function's parameter is `E0877` at the parameter, because a call through `callable` passes one argument for each parameter — `rule:types/anonymous-function`
--FILE--
<?nvs
callable $count = fn(int ...$xs): int => Core\Arr::count($xs) as int;
callable $three = fn(int $x = 3): int => $x;
callable(int): int $twice = fn(int $x): int => $x * 2;

echo $twice(4), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0877]: the anonymous function's parameter `$xs` takes exactly one argument
%A
2 | callable $count = fn(int ...$xs): int => Core\Arr::count($xs) as int;
  |                             ^^^ declared with `...` here
  = help: remove the `...`. To pass many values, declare an `array<T>` parameter and pass one array

error[E0877]: the anonymous function's parameter `$x` takes exactly one argument
%A
3 | callable $three = fn(int $x = 3): int => $x;
  |                               ^ a default value here
  = help: remove the default, and pass the value in every call

error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
